an increased army presence on the  streets in el salvador an immediate  reaction to a bloody weekend 62  homicides on saturday the most in one  single day in more than 20 years  the president and congress passing a  temporary move to impose restrictions on  assembly extend police detentions and  allow the intercept of communications  like phone calls  the decree that declares the emergency  regime is approved  el salvador is home to several violent  gangs while president native buchelli  has been credited with cutting the crime  rate it's still one of the most violent  countries on earth he tweeted his  approval of the assembly's endorsement  of his move saying the measures to be  taken will be implemented by the  pertinent institutions and announced  only when it's necessary for the  majority of the population life  continues as normal may god bless us all  many on the streets of san salvador  backed the move  i think it's good because it's excellent  if we can look out for each other let  him show he is against crime that's all  i can say  i think the approval is good because  there's too much violence and injustice  happening everything had calmed down but  this is revenge against the government  if it was in my hands i would give them  a harsh penalty as they say a brutal  punishment  president because previously been  accused of negotiating a truce with the  gangs to win their political support  something he denies  the new restrictions are in place for 30  days  but could be extended alan fisher al  jazeera
 

